Non-cubic uniform dark-matter zoom example.

This example is identical to UniformDMGravity except the high-resolution
particle region is twice as long along the z axis as it is along x and y. The
zoom region is padded independently along each axis, so it is not a cube: it
spans 2x2x4 background top-level cells.

The setup has been tuned for a zoom-region with:

- ZoomRegion:bkg_top_level_cells = 8,
- ZoomRegion:zoom_top_level_depth = 2,
- a zoom extent that spans the central 2x2x4 background cells, giving 8x8x16
  zoom top-level cells.

Run with the --zoom runtime option.
